WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.980
It's hard to watch this.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.690
Bring me a new song immediately!

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:04.490
Damn!

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:05.560
You can't be serious!

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.800
If you don't take good care of people, 
someday you'll make a huge mistake.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.780
I'll crush them completely.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.400
Both Takanashi Productions and his daughter.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.450
And IDOLiSH7!

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.320
Huh?! What the hell is this trying to say?!

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.870
What's with this crap? It's pissing me off!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.750
Tamaki-kun, even magazines rile you up.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.460
Take a look at this!

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.170
Mitsuki-san's interview?

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.960
<b>MEZZO" is IDOLiSH7's Reserve Group?!</b>

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:27.960
This is...

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.420
See? Doesn't it piss you off?

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:41.180
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.730
Someday we'll make it past there

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:50.310
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.160
We don't know what's right

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.380
So we Try and Jump!

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:03.540
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.170
For us It's Only Way!

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.340
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.820
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:16.340
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.510
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.340
Live! (Yeah!)

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.760
In the light!

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.560
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:29.020
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.810
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.330
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:41.830
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:48.790
The future surely lies on the other side

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.710
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.090
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:01.350
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:13.780
I'm exhausted.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.350
Yeah.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:20.280
Lately we've stopped gathering 
here as a group, though.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.200
Yeah, we've been getting 
a lot more individual jobs.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.160
I'm glad we have work, 
but it's kind of lonely.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.210
Yeah.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:36.380
Oh, well. I wonder what 
everyone's doing today.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.780
<b>Yotsuba Tamaki
 </b>I'm tiiired. 

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:37.940
<b>Hero Info 
</b>The next episode of Covert Squad Secret Rangers,
 "The Mysterious Object in Snow Country! 
Working Together" will take place in Tohoku! 
The object will be important to the story arc.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.380
♥Osaka Sogo-san likes this<b>
 Tidiness Tips
 </b>Tips for keeping a tidier room. A must read for anyone 
who wants to be tidy and organized! "How to sort 
things that are and aren't important."

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.380
<b>Ainana@I7 Riku Fan</b>

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.320
Ainana@I7 Riku Fan

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.320
@NanaseRiku-san
 Is this true? How awful!

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.340
How do you feel about Nanase 
Riku-san's abilities as a center?

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.340
<b>[Izumi]  Nanase-san is weak. 
We can't rely on him as our center.</b>

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.340
Iori-san, you seem like you'd be the more 
reliable member within your group.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.350
What?

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.180
That jerk...

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.380
What's wrong?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.900
Uh, nothing.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.580
I guess he says that all the time, though.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.080
By the way, Riku...

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:57.730
Huh?

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.100
Have you talked to Yamato-san recently?

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.630
No. He's been busy filming, I think.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.750
Haven't seen him much at the dorm, either.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.860
I see.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.450
What about him, though?

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:12.440
The other day I heard 
from the TV station staff

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:17.300
that Yamato-san's thinking about quitting 
being an idol and focusing on acting.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.090
Huh?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.300
What is this?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.050
<b>MyuMyu ~ Aggregator</b>

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.050
<b>"Our Failure at Music Festa was Iori's Fault"</b>

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.050
Source: [Your Music Show Report] 
Rising indie artist fails to perform?

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.980
Well, I'm sure he'd say that
 without any malice, though.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.150
Good morning.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.760
Hey, Iori.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.140
Sorry. I'm heading back.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:38.810
Nii-san.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:40.900
What's wrong?

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.820
Did you guys get into a fight?

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:44.920
No, we didn't.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.660
You got into the group 
riding Iori's coattails?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.310
Did Iori say that?

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.490
It was in an online article.

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.630
Then it's not true.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:02.930
When I asked Banri-san, 
he said it was true at first.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.520
But he added that if the president 
hadn't seen my potential,

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.750
I couldn't have joined the group.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.210
I feel stupid.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:22.660
I was so excited to be accepted, 
but it was on his strength.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.360
Mitsuki, we need you.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.340
You're an important member.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.250
Even if you guys feel that way, 
he thinks I'm an added bonus.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:36.250
Mitsuki, are you being serious?

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.610
Of course not.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.260
After all, he's my younger brother.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.060
Why is he my younger brother?

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:51.460
I've felt this way since we were kids.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.390
I've had enough.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.420
Mitsuki...

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.530
<b>Driver's License</b>

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.530
I finally acquired a driver's license!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.800
<b>Driver's License</b>

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.110
From now on, I'll be taking 
you to and from work.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:11.320
Thanks for making time in your busy 
schedule to do this for us, Manager.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.290
We'll have to celebrate properly soon.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.210
Now, get in.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.460
Sorry, but I'm not sitting next to Tama.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.130
Huh? Why not?

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:25.090
Ask yourself that question.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.130
Huh?!

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.130
Did you do something again?

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.600
Why do you assume it was Tamaki-kun's fault?

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.560
Huh?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.480
Because Yotsuba-san is more 
likely to have done something.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.330
Right, Nii-san?

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.560
Hey, I didn't ask you to back me up.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.110
Are you that desperate to 
make me look like a dumbass?

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.110
I wasn't trying to...

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.400
Iori's always doing that to people, though.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.310
What does that mean?

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:51.090
Oh, this won't do at all.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.100
Iori, we have something important to discuss.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.680
Something important?

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.680
Wasn't this originally about
 Nikaido-san and Yotsuba-san?

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.370
Forget it. No need to bring it up again.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.500
What's with the attitude?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:04.430
It's pissing me off!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:09.290
It's your fault for saying I have something 
to do with someone in show business!

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.870
What?! I never said that!

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.290
Tamaki, stop!

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.320
Again, you're only scolding Tamaki-kun?

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.730
Is it because we're the reserve group?

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.250
Reserve?

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.770
It's because he's picking a fight.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:23.880
Iori, people's hearts are very delicate.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.250
They are hurt by the smallest things.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.040
Okay?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.400
What? I'm less worried about hearts

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.530
and more worried that 
Nikaido-san's about to get hit.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:31.960
Huh?

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.700
No, no!

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.700
It's true that Tamaki-kun and I are...

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.700
Please stop!

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.960
Wh-What's going on, everyone?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.010
What are you talking about?!

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.010
I don't know!

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:40.960
More importantly...

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:47.970
Get in the car, now!

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.220
<b>Mr. Shimooka's 
The TV Man Show</b>

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.440
<i>I hear the special drama you're filming</i>

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.240
<i>is a spin-off of a show 
that aired previously.</i>

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:53.850
<i>Yes.</i>

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.800
They're so cute.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:56.950
I know.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.850
What's wrong?

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.270
Don't they seem a little down?

00:07:01.790 --> 00:07:03.050
Do they?

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.400
I guess they might, 
now that you mention it.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.670
They've been getting more work recently,

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.200
so maybe they're just tired.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.810
You think so?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.080
You think it's because of 
magazines and online articles?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.560
They're mixing truths and lies.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.960
It's awful.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.960
It feels like there's been 
a sudden increase in them.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.930
Maybe it's just a symptom 
of their new popularity.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.930
I think their packed 
schedules is a factor.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.770
There's MEZZO" of course, and 
Yamato-san is filming for his drama.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.140
Nagi-san is modeling.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.350
Riku-san and Iori-san are 
getting a lot of exposure, too.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.110
Mitsuki-san's been appearing 
on more variety shows.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.110
I'm not sure they're getting many 
chances to talk to each other.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:54.360
Before, they'd hang out in the lesson 
room even when they had nothing to do.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.870
We need to do something.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.850
I'll get it.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.450
Excuse me. Thanks for waiting.

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:06.630
Hello.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.580
Oh, the soba deliveryman.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:11.150
Huh? We haven't ordered anything today...

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.370
I'm not from the soba shop.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.160
Huh?

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.570
What? Then...

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:15.550
Do you have a minute?

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:16.260
It won't take long.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.720
Huh? Huh? What?!

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.730
Sorry for dragging you out here.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:27.980
It's fine. Um, you're really
 Yaotome-san, right?

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.690
No one else is this handsome, are they?

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.520
I want to ask you something 
about your father.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:39.740
My da—the president?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:42.130
Apparently he knew my dad.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:44.500
Huh? President Yaotome?

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.390
My parents are divorced.

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:52.630
My mom always said my dad 
loved another woman.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.680
I thought he was having an affair,

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.890
but the other day I heard him 
arguing with your father.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.520
I could've made her happier!

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:08.510
Is Musubi your mother?

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:11.780
Yes, although she died when I was a child.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.330
I see.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.250
Huh?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.930
Huh?! Y-Yaotome-san?

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.020
Call me Gaku.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:32.330
I-I can't do that!

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.050
Why not?

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:33.880
Huh?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.490
Uh, G-Gaku-san?

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.380
Yeah.

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:41.030
Thanks for filling in for us the other day.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.480
Huh? Oh, no problem.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.380
I envy you.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.770
You're free to do what you 
want. You're having fun.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.490
There's no reason to envy us.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.150
Everyone always aspires to be like TRIGGER.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:57.740
Hey, I heard you sang our new song perfectly.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.320
Yes. They always loved the song.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:03.910
Before we went to Okinawa,
 they had the choreography perf—

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.990
Okinawa?

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:06.590
Oh, never mind.

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:09.710
We met in Okinawa before 
our song was released.

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.210
How did you know about it before then?

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.210
Because...

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:15.610
Tenn said something strange, too.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.430
He asked if we were really happy.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:19.760
It's nothing. I was mistaken.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.340
Are you sure something didn't happen?

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.430
Please, tell me.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:23.930
Stop!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.400
You're upsetting her!

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.350
Wait, Yaotome Gaku?

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.670
Stay out of this.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.270
I was talking to Tsumugi.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:32.420
Not "Tsumugi<i>-san</i>"?

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.610
You're upsetting our manager!

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.770
I'm fine.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:39.270
Then you answer my question, Nanase Riku.

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:42.320
How did the seven of you 
sing that song perfectly?

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:45.240
Well?

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:47.080
Riku-san.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.020
It was stolen.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:48.760
What?

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:51.310
By your music producer.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.130
The demo tape for our song was stolen.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.130
Riku-san!

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.520
That was originally our debut song.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.470
We even shot a PV in Okinawa.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.340
Is that true?

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.160
I wouldn't lie about this.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:13.290
We were singing a song we stole from you?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.360
A stolen song? But...

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:22.050
TRIGGER's members aren't responsible!

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.160
You didn't know anything.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:27.350
You're very kind.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.040
Sorry about the sudden visit.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:32.520
Thanks for talking to me.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:36.680
Bye.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:42.210
Manager, are you okay?

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.550
The thief is the one in the wrong.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.020
TRIGGER didn't have to know.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:53.410
Sorry. I shouldn't have done that.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:57.020
Why were you with him?

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.110
Because...

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.240
If you don't want to tell me, that's okay.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:02.740
It's not what you think.

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:06.900
It's about his family,
so I can't go into detail.

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:08.910
Excuse me.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:12.490
Hello? This is Takanashi.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.100
Huh?

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.340
Yes. Yes.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.880
Let's hurry back to the office.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.160
<b>The Disowned Son of a Noble?! 
The Truth Behind MEZZO"'s Osaka Sogo!</b>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.870
<b>The Hunt for His Sister Was A Lie?! 
Endless "Manufactured Sympathy"</b>

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.880
What is this?

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.870
<b>Members Tell All!
MEZZO" is IDOLiSH7's Reserve Group</b>

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.080
It's all lies!

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:26.740
This is malicious.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:27.600
I'll submit complaints.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.590
There's no point in complaining.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:32.930
Unless you take them to court, 
they won't print an apology.

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:35.860
Will Tenn-nii deny it?

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:38.230
I doubt he'd comment on these articles.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.690
Most people won't believe them.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.530
But if someone does...

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:45.380
Sogo-kun's family situation 
has been exposed, too.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.650
They haven't named the company, though.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:48.910
It's not just me.

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:51.190
They're claiming Tamaki-kun's 
search for his sister

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.590
is a lie he's spreading for publicity.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:54.960
They can't be serious!

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:58.420
"A major actor is suspected 
of having a secret lovechild,

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.410
and that child is IDOLiSH7's Nikaido Yamato?"

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:01.960
Huh?

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.140
Th-That's obviously not true.

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.890
Can you believe the nonsense they write?

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:09.720
This one has an article on Rokuya-san.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:14.550
"The idol everyone's been talking about 
is actually a Scandinavian prince?"

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:15.980
Okay!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:16.680
That's a lie.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:17.650
It sure is.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:21.610
Information about Iori-san and 
Mitsuki-san's family is circulating, too.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.270
Our family works in the service industry.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.080
That should be good advertising for them.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:25.820
But...

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.820
We're prepared for this.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.770
After all, we joined the 
entertainment industry.

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:32.040
Don't let this set you on edge.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.290
We're not!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:36.750
Anyway, there are too 
many malicious articles.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.290
Someone could be pulling strings behind this.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.340
What?

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:48.340
Takanashi should be realizing his 
own powerlessness around now.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.530
Even when people encounter 
something wonderful,

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.910
once they discover its 
shortcomings, they despair.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.070
The dream ends, and it slowly loses value.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:03.110
More than anything, I doubt their 
spirits will be able to keep up.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.640
Rage, sadness...

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.610
Eventually they'll lose the will to
 bestow dreams upon their fans.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.010
Soon it'll be checkmate.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.500
Prepare yourself, Takanashi.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.170
<b>Cold</b>

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.550
Oh, him?

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.450
The alleged impostor?

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:27.670
People will do anything for fame.

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:29.570
Tamaki-kun.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.350
Mister.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.660
Great timing.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:35.210
Huh?

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.600
We're going to be filming that show.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:38.500
Huh?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.850
That show?

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.240
An emotional reunion?

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.820
That's happening after filming today?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:51.070
Yes. Tamaki-san previously promised 
the director that he'd do the show.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.580
It's sudden, but they're 
going to be filming today.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.370
Is it to find your younger sister?

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:02.420
Yeah. They said they'd use 
the show's money to find her.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.790
Should we be doing this right now?

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:07.480
I don't care if people say I'm faking.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.630
I'd do anything to see her.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:13.250
They haven't told you they found her?

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.140
They'd keep that secret to 
get his candid reaction.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:20.890
I hope they found your sister.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:22.710
Yeah.

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:25.930
Yes?

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:29.740
IDOLiSH7, get on standby, please.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:30.400
Okay.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.660
His mother passed away, 
and his father is missing.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:45.040
He hasn't seen his sister since 
they lived at the orphanage.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.040
<b>A Moving Reunion Special</b>

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.810
His days were full of pain and loneliness.

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:51.300
Yotsuba Tamaki-kun, it's time 
for your emotional reunion.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.090
Reunion?

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:54.960
They found your sister?

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.860
That's great, Tamaki-kun.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:57.920
Aya.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:00.310
Let's have him come onstage now.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.650
You haven't seen him since you were three.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:04.480
This is Tamaki-kun's father.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:11.820
Unfortunately, we were unable to find your
 sister, but our staff located your father.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.110
Thanks for having me.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.570
What do you think of your son, all grown up?

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.990
How do you feel seeing your son again?

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.910
He's grown into a fine young man.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:23.370
He looks just like I used to.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.580
I'm so proud of my son.

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:35.170
Tamaki-kun?!

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:38.120
How dare you show up here, 
you good-for-nothing bastard?!

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.060
Tamaki-kun.

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:44.200
Because of you, mom died, 
and Aya and I got separated!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:45.480
T-Tamaki, your dad—

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:46.810
Shut up!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:47.650
Stop!

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.440
Let go of me, you piece of shit!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.150
Shimooka-san!

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.800
Tama, we get it! We get it!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.800
T-Tamaki-kun!

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:57.410
Don't!

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.410
Damn. Damn it!

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:03.090
Sheesh.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:05.300
It's okay.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:09.330
It's okay. Calm down.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:15.610
Tamaki-kun.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:17.930
Stop the recording!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.950
I'm sure there's some reason for this.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:24.690
Maybe the studio's at fault, but you're
 all supposed to be professionals!

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.350
Why can't shoot a show like this!

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:28.630
We're sorry.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:29.650
We're sorry!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.150
We're sorry!

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:37.650
You should apologize to the staff, not me.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:44.290
No way. I'm not apologizing.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:49.590
Why the hell not?! Our manager's off 
desperately apologizing for you right now!

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:51.460
Whatever the circumstances,

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.290
you stopped filming on a show 
several people were involved in.

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.590
You even injured Shimooka-san!

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.260
I still won't do it.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:00.640
You chose to take this job,

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:01.670
so take responsibility!

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:05.400
I did it because they said they'd find Aya.

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:08.600
But they brought that
 bastard here instead.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:11.880
Yamato-san, we should go apologize.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.610
We can't go without the guy who hurt him.

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:18.490
If this had been live, our 
group would be disbanded.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:19.990
Disband us, then!

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:24.700
Are you serio—

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:25.750
Wait.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:28.350
Think about how Tamaki-kun feels.

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:30.920
He hasn't collected his thoughts yet.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.890
If my father came out like 
that, I'd get chills, too.

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.500
Wouldn't you, Yamato-san?

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:37.800
I don't know what you mean.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.380
I read the article.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.850
You're the secret lovechild of 
someone big in show business.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:44.330
I said it's a lie.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.560
I don't believe you.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.310
That's irrelevant right now!

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:49.400
No! No, no.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:51.190
Please don't fight.

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.480
We're dear friends.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.200
Teammates. Isn't that right?

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:02.890
Why won't anyone answer me?

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:04.990
It's an emergency!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.060
I just got the call.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:15.750
IDOLiSH7 has been nominated for the Japan 
Idol Music Awards' new artist award!

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:20.760
Guys?

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:28.270
Ryu, Tenn. There's something 
I have to tell you first.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.930
Why do you look so serious?

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:33.400
I may be forced to quit TRIGGER.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:37.190
I'm gonna go punch my dad.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.810
Hey, wait!

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:39.240
Let go!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.810
Cool your head.

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:48.840
Could you leave us and our fans 
out of your family dispute?

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.540
Family has nothing to do with it!

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:52.790
What happened?

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:55.220
You guys don't need to know.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:57.240
I'm going to settle this.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:59.480
Don't be so secretive. We're—

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:01.340
Just business partners.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.850
We're friends who have 
always worked together!

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:11.850
We made it this far by covering for each 
other's mistakes and celebrating together!

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.350
I think of us as friends!

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.440
I feel an even stronger bond between us!

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:18.550
Tell us, Gaku.

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.610
And Tenn, don't say things you don't mean.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:27.080
We've been singing a song 
stolen from IDOLiSH7.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.740
A stolen song?

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.290
Apparently Hyuga Akihito did it.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.960
If it was on my dad's orders, I'm not 
gonna be able to hold myself back.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.790
I thought so.

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:41.970
You noticed? Why didn't you say anything?!

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:44.180
Is that all your pride is worth?!

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:44.180
Gaku.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:51.600
I didn't say anything because
 I didn't want to see you two hurt.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:57.590
You said you liked the song.
 That you enjoyed it.

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:00.040
If you learned it was stolen,

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:04.090
I thought you'd feel too pathetic 
and embarrassed to sing it!

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.090
Tenn.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:09.490
You're right, Gaku. I sacrificed my pride.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:12.150
I prioritized my emotions 
and pretended not to notice.

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:17.380
Business partners don't need
 friendship, after all.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:30.020
Tenn, I need to confirm something with you.

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:32.200
Oh, my. What a strange atmosphere.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.270
What is it?

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.250
It's about gossip.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:38.150
You should've told me you 
and Nanase Riku were twins.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:42.560
We've been caught in the crossfire of the 
destruction of another agency's performers.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:43.940
Destruction of performers?

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:45.380
Manager.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:46.390
What now?

00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:51.800
I told you after <i>Sound Ship</i> that if you 
embarrassed us in front of our fans again,

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.950
that I had some ideas.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:57.710
Now that you remember 
that, answer me honestly.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:04.290
Did the media just find out that 
Riku's my twin, or were they <i>told?</i>

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:17.950
Start running (beyond)

00:22:17.950 --> 00:22:24.960
Your imagination... Alive

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:38.610
If you desire something from 
the bottom of your heart

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:43.250
Risk your life and dive in

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:48.340
The resolve to discard what's truly important

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:53.470
Is the boat that will take you to new sights

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:56.020
(Hey man!) Take the strings of your heart

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:58.560
(Hey man!) And stretch them

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:01.440
(Say dream!) To the limit

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:06.360
At the other end you're sure 
to find the Gate to paradise

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:12.450
You'll be the first witness

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:17.240
Our pounding pulses are Heavenly

00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:22.530
Admit that you can't deny it

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:26.920
We start... What do your fingertips

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:31.260
Seek now?

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:50.940
Congratulations on being nominated 
for the JIMA new artist award!

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:52.570
<b>Congratulations! 
JIMA New Artist Award Nomination!!</b>

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:53.850
This is a fantastic achievement, guys!

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:58.410
You're not happy?

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:02.550
Looks like you're not in 
the mood to celebrate.

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:04.200
Sir.

00:24:05.430 --> 00:24:10.280
If you feel no happiness when what 
you've been striving for is within reach,

00:24:10.820 --> 00:24:12.770
then it's no longer your dream.

00:24:13.240 --> 00:24:15.050
You should quit being idols.

00:24:16.410 --> 00:24:17.560
Sir.

00:24:19.060 --> 00:24:21.560
IDOLiSH7 is disbanded.

00:24:22.070 --> 00:24:23.510
MEZZO" is also disbanded.

00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:25.730
Thank you for your work.

00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:31.500
Closing Doors
